  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124511,
      "id": "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "88b667ff-8e36-549d-8e05-205078cc261a",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and  $det(A)=-2?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is not invertible\n\n- **II.** $\\text{rank}(A)=5$\n\n- **III.** $A$ has $6$ pivot columns",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-2\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be  invertible.\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\text{rank}(A)=6.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=6$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $6$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4477acad-b3f0-5f49-bc4c-3d36f232ce64",
