  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124511,
      "id": "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "95b99ecd-e82a-5f48-8955-35c9cd1ca717",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "21eb13b5-9676-5f51-ba31-c3b8d1747dcb",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "e3becd45-905e-5d1c-8429-4d6f8ec2addb",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ccc09394-0758-58e7-86f9-978c38eb2518",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "I only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "07bd8153-36ef-561a-b843-7810a34d0b3c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "III only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "2e19e846-cbcc-5033-b98b-d3e7b18ad5ae",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "II and III only"
            },
            {
